WEBVTT

01
00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:13.089
This is Open rows, a version of Value rows. The rows you open stay open, so restyling shape after shape takes one click per change.

02
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:20.006
Select a shape, and each property shows its current value in a field you can open.

03
00:00:20.456 --> 00:00:30.852
Quick style, at the top, sets how a shape is filled and drawn. Its styles have plain names, like Lines, Crossed lines and Filled.

04
00:00:32.185 --> 00:00:34.396
Open Stroke, and pick green.

05
00:00:35.297 --> 00:00:40.246
Open Background as well. Stroke stays open, so both are right there.

06
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.849
Edges goes from round to sharp. Close it, and the other two stay open.

07
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:53.513
Now select the ellipse. Stroke and Background are still open, so each change is one click.

08
00:00:53.915 --> 00:00:57.097
Then the diamond, one click each.

09
00:00:58.199 --> 00:01:02.847
The full palette, with shades and a hex code, opens inside the row.

10
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:10.454
Stroke width, Fill, Stroke style, Sloppiness and Opacity open in place too.

11
00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.351
Layers and the actions stay at the bottom, however many rows are open.

12
00:01:22.653 --> 00:01:25.657
When you're done, Close all puts every row away.

13
00:01:27.875 --> 00:01:39.664
What works well: the rows you use stay open from shape to shape, each change after that is one click, and the rest of the panel still reads as a short summary.

14
00:01:40.365 --> 00:01:48.305
What's harder: the first change still takes two clicks, a lot of open rows make the panel tall again, and closing them is up to you.
